Explanation:
 We mostly ban packages in prisonpc-bad-package-conflicts-everyone.
 This works well, and we get clear error messages.
 But it cannot block virtual packages, and it cannot block a glob of package names.
 In here, block things that prisonpc-bad-package-conflicts-everyone can't.
 .
 If you try to install a package blocked here,
 the error message will be something like this:
     E: Package 'libc6-dev' has no installation candidate
 .
 One benefit of blocking things explicitly here is that measure-install-footprints.py
 will skip them before measuring them, i.e. runs faster.
 .
 Use an arbitrary negative number instead of -1, so
 it is easier to git grep for that number across the codebase,
 when you see it in apt policy output.
Pin-Priority: -17751
Pin: version *
Package:
 *-dev
 *-dbg
 *-dbgsym
 src:debian-installer-netboot-images
 src:7zip
